There isn't a direct `IsPostBack` equivalent in JavaScript, since PostBack is a server-side concept that belongs to ASP.NET.

However, you can use sessions, cookies or HTML5 localStorage to check if the page has been loaded before. 

One possible solution could be:

```javascript
window.onload = function(){
    if(!localStorage.getItem("loaded"))
    {
        // This is a first time load .. do your stuff here
        alert("This is a first time load ...");

        // set local storage item 
        localStorage.setItem("loaded", true);
    }
    else
    {
        // This is a load by postback .. do nothing or do other stuff here
        alert("This is a load by Postback");
    }
};
```

Remember that this will work only in browsers that support localStorage (IE8+, and all versions of Chrome, Firefox, and Opera).

If you are using ASP.NET and want to call JS functions from the server side, you can add a property to the body tag to check for PostBack:

```javascript
<body <%=Page.IsPostBack ? "data-ispostback='true'" : "data-ispostback='false'";%>>
```

Then, on your JavaScript code you can do:

```javascript
window.onload = function() {
    var isPostback = document.body.getAttribute('data-ispostback') === 'true';
    if (!isPostback) {
